    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **262 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `capacityWarning` flag on the owner response so it returns `true` when the owner's city already holds 40\u201349 owners (approaching the hard limit of 50), leaving the existing 409 rejection at 50 untouched.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `capacityWarning` boolean property to the owner schema (alongside `bulkSignupWarning`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field and its setter.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added `@Mapping(target = \"capacityWarning\", ignore = true)` since the value is computed in the controller rather than mapped from the entity (matching how `bulkSignupWarning` is handled).\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 added a `capacityWarning(String city)` helper that counts owners in the city the same way the hard-limit rule does (all owners with a matching normalized city) and returns `true` for a count in `[40, 49]`. It's set on the DTO in all three response-building paths: `getOwner` (the asserted read-back), the idempotent-replay path in `addOwner`, and the normal create path. The hard rejection (`ownersInCity >= 50` \u2192 409) is unchanged.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreWarnsWhenApproachingCapacity` passes, and the full existing suite remains green.",
